.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NVIDIA_DRM_RENDER 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvidia_drm_render
.Nd render interface of the nvidia-drm driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nvidia-drm-render.h
.Pp
.Ft int
.Fn ioctl "int fd" "unsigned long request" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The render interface (NVR) lets a user-space graphics driver use the GPU
through the DRM
device that
.Nm nvidia-drm
creates.
It is shaped like the render interface of the nouveau driver, so that a
Vulkan driver written for that model needs only a small backend.
The numbers and the semantics are the driver's own.
The interface is available on both the render node and the card node, needs no
.Dv DRM_MASTER ,
and is safe to call from any number of threads on one descriptor.
.Pp
A descriptor is one client.
It owns one GPU virtual address space, created by
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_INIT ,
a set of buffer objects named by GEM handles, and a set of channels.
A channel is an in-order queue on one GPU engine.
Buffers are memory only: they get a GPU address when
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_BIND
maps them.
Jobs are ordered with DRM syncobjs, which are created and passed by the core
DRM ioctls, not by this interface.
.Pp
The header defines the version in
.Dv NVR_UAPI_VERSION_MAJOR
and
.Dv NVR_UAPI_VERSION_MINOR .
The major version is 1.
A caller must refuse a major version it does not know.
A larger minor version only adds
.Dv GETPARAM
values, flag bits that older callers leave zero, and ioctls.
.Pp
Every structure uses fixed-width types and no pointers, a user pointer being a
.Vt uint64_t .
There is no implicit padding, every 64-bit member sits at a multiple of 8, and
every structure size is a multiple of 8, so 32-bit and 64-bit callers see the
same layout.
Padding, reserved members and unknown flag bits must be zero, or the call
fails with
.Er EINVAL .
A call that fails changes nothing.
.Sh IOCTLS
Command numbers are relative to
.Dv DRM_COMMAND_BASE .
They are in the range 0x45 to 0x5f, above the numbers of the
.Dv DRM_NVIDIA_*
ioctls of the same driver and of the nouveau driver's ioctls.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_GETPARAM Pq 0x45, Vt struct drm_nvr_getparam
Return one parameter.
.Va param
is an
.Dv NVR_PARAM_*
value and
.Va value
the result.
The parameters are the interface version, PCI device, the limits (pushes per
exec, channels, bind operations, synchronisation entries), video memory size,
BAR size,
the video memory this descriptor holds and the free video memory
(rounded down to a multiple of 16 MiB), the GPU timer in nanoseconds,
the GPC and TPC counts, the
virtual address width and limit, the smallest kernel range for
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_INIT ,
the GPU page sizes and the feature flags.
An unknown parameter is
.Er EINVAL .
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_GETINFO Pq 0x46, Vt struct drm_nvr_getinfo
Return the device identity, chip, compute topology, memory sizes, limits, a
name and the list of GPU classes.
The class list is written to the array at
.Va classes_ptr ,
at most
.Va classes_cap
entries; the full count is returned in
.Va classes_count .
.Va classes_ptr
must be 0 when
.Va classes_cap
is 0 and non-zero otherwise, so call once with both 0 to get the count.
.Va flags
reports
.Dv NVR_INFO_FLAG_NO_VRAM
(unified memory, no video memory),
.Dv NVR_INFO_FLAG_CPU_COHERENT ,
.Dv NVR_INFO_FLAG_BAR_DEVICE_MEM
and
.Dv NVR_INFO_FLAG_COMPRESSION .
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_CHANNEL_ALLOC Pq 0x47, Vt struct drm_nvr_channel_alloc
Create a channel on an engine
.Pq Dv NVR_ENGINE_GR , NVR_ENGINE_CE , NVR_ENGINE_NVDEC , NVR_ENGINE_NVENC .
.Va engine_instance
for
.Dv NVR_ENGINE_CE
is 0 to let the driver choose, or 1 to the
.Va ce_count
returned by
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_GETINFO
to select that copy engine; the numbering is 1-based.
For every other engine it must be 0.
The driver creates the engine objects and returns them, with their
subchannels, in
.Va objs .
Needs
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_INIT
first.
Channel numbers are never reused within one descriptor.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_CHANNEL_FREE Pq 0x48, Vt struct drm_nvr_channel_free
Invalidate a channel number at once.
Running jobs finish, fail or time out; every job not yet handed to the
hardware, whether it waits for a fence or only for the jobs ahead of it, is
cancelled with
.Er ECANCELED
on its signal fences.
The driver then destroys the channel in the GPU's resource manager and only
then releases its memory.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_GEM_NEW Pq 0x49, Vt struct drm_nvr_gem_new
Create a buffer object.
.Va domain
is a mask of
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM ,
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_GART ,
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_MAPPABLE ,
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_COHERENT
and
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_NO_SHARE ;
at least one of the first two is required.
The returned
.Va domain
tells where the memory was placed, and the placement never changes.
On a device without video memory a video memory request is placed in coherent
system memory.
.Va pte_kind
is checked against the device and
.Va tile_mode
is stored without interpretation.
A call with neither
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM
nor
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_GART ,
or with
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_COHERENT
and video memory only on a device that has video memory, fails with
.Er EINVAL .
A buffer with
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_NO_SHARE
cannot be exported, by PRIME or by flink: the call fails with
.Er EPERM .
.Va map_handle
is the offset to pass to
.Xr mmap 2
on the descriptor.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_GEM_INFO Pq 0x4a, Vt struct drm_nvr_gem_info
Return the same information for an existing handle.
.Va flags
and
.Va pad
must be zero.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_GEM_CPU_PREP Pq 0x4b, Vt struct drm_nvr_gem_cpu_prep
Wait until the GPU has finished with the buffer for the kind of CPU access
requested
.Pq Dv NVR_GEM_CPU_PREP_WRITE ,
or fail with
.Er EBUSY
when
.Dv NVR_GEM_CPU_PREP_NOWAIT
is set.
If a job that the call waited for faulted, the call fails with
.Er ENODEV :
the GPU is finished with the buffer but its contents are unspecified, so
rewrite or discard them.
The job's own signal fences report the fault too.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_GEM_CPU_FINI Pq 0x4c, Vt struct drm_nvr_gem_cpu_fini
End a CPU access window.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_INIT Pq 0x4d, Vt struct drm_nvr_vm_init
Choose the part of the GPU address space the kernel keeps for itself (at least
the
.Dv NVR_PARAM_KERNEL_VA_MIN_SIZE
value, never below 16 MiB, 2 MiB aligned, inside the address space).
The rest is the caller's.
Call it once, before the first channel or bind.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_BIND Pq 0x4e, Vt struct drm_nvr_vm_bind
Apply a list of map and unmap operations
.Pq Va op_ptr , op_count .
A map places a range of a buffer at a GPU address.
A map with
.Dv NVR_VM_BIND_SPARSE
makes a sparse region where reads return zero and writes are dropped.
An unmap may cut a mapping; inside a sparse region the cut part becomes sparse
again.
All operations of one call are validated in order and applied together, or not
at all.
Without
.Dv NVR_VM_BIND_RUN_ASYNC
the call returns when the page tables are updated.
With it the bind is queued on the descriptor's bind queue, which runs in
order, waits for all entries of
.Va wait_ptr
and signals all entries of
.Va sig_ptr
when done.
Memory needed for the update is reserved when the call is accepted.
.It Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_EXEC Pq 0x4f, Vt struct drm_nvr_exec
Submit one job to a channel: a list of push buffer ranges in the GPU address
space (each at most
.Dv NVR_EXEC_PUSH_LEN_MAX
bytes, 8 MiB less 4), with wait and signal syncobjs.
A waiting syncobj must already hold a fence.
Jobs on one channel run in order.
It does not wait for earlier asynchronous binds unless a syncobj says so.
It sleeps when the channel's ring is full.
A call with no pushes, waits or signals is a liveness probe.
.El
.Sh CPU MAPPINGS
A mapped buffer gets its attribute from where its memory is, not from what the
caller asks for.
Video memory is reached through a PCIe BAR and is never cacheable.
On Ampere Altra systems it is mapped Device-nGnRE, and
.Dv NVR_INFO_FLAG_BAR_DEVICE_MEM
is set: the caller must then use naturally aligned accesses and no atomic
operations on it.
System memory is mapped Normal write-back for a coherent buffer on a device
with
.Dv NVR_INFO_FLAG_CPU_COHERENT ,
and Normal non-cacheable otherwise.
A device attribute is never put on RAM, and a RAM attribute never on a BAR.
Do not use
.Xr memcpy 3
or
.Xr memset 3
on a mapping with
.Dv NVR_INFO_FLAG_BAR_DEVICE_MEM :
copy with aligned 4-byte or 8-byte loads and stores, or stage the data in a
system memory buffer.
A mapping may not extend past its buffer, and only a descriptor that holds a
handle to the buffer can map it: on any other descriptor
.Xr mmap 2
fails with
.Er EACCES ,
so import the buffer with PRIME first.
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_EXEC
issues a store barrier before it publishes work.
.Sh ERRORS
Each ioctl returns 0 on success and \-1 with
.Va errno
set on failure.
The errors are:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EINVAL
A value, flag, alignment or range rule was broken, a reserved bit was set, or
the call came in the wrong state, for example
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_CHANNEL_ALLOC
or
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_BIND
before
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_INIT .
.It Er E2BIG
A count is above its limit.
.It Er EFAULT
A user pointer cannot be read or written.
.It Er ENOENT
The handle, channel or mapping does not exist.
.It Er EEXIST
A map overlaps an existing mapping.
.It Er EBUSY
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_INIT
was already called on this descriptor, a sparse region still has mappings, or
.Dv NVR_GEM_CPU_PREP_NOWAIT
was given and the buffer is busy; retry without the flag to wait.
.It Er ENOMEM
Memory is exhausted.
For a buffer with
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM
and
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_MAPPABLE
it can mean that the CPU-visible part of video memory is used up: allocate
without
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_MAPPABLE
and copy, or use
.Dv NVR_GEM_DOMAIN_GART .
A buffer with a compressed
.Va pte_kind
never falls back to system memory.
.It Er ENOSPC
The per-descriptor channel limit is reached (channels that were freed but are
still draining count against it), or the limit of queued binds and jobs that
have not started, or of the page-table memory they reserve, is reached.
Wait for draining channels or queued work to start or finish, and retry.
If no channel is draining, the descriptor has used up its channel numbers or
its kernel range: open the device again.
.It Er EPERM
The buffer cannot be shared.
.It Er ENODEV
The channel or the GPU is lost.
A channel that faults, or runs past the job timeout, is lost: the failing
job and every job behind it complete with this error, later calls on the
channel return it, and other channels and descriptors are not affected.
Free the channel with
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_CHANNEL_FREE
and create a new one.
When the whole GPU is lost, creating channels and
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_NVR_VM_BIND
return it as well, and the descriptor must be closed and opened again.
.It Er EINTR
A sleep was interrupted; nothing was changed.
Retry the call.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr memcpy 3
.Pp
.Pa docs/RENDER-UAPI.md
in the nvidia-gb10-freebsd repository
.Pq github.com/cloudbsdorg/nvidia-gb10-freebsd ,
for every argument, ordering rule and limit, and
.Pa src/nvidia-drm-render/nvidia-drm-render.h
for the structures.
.Sh HISTORY
The render interface first appeared in the CloudBSD build of nvidia-drm in
2026.
